{0 statements}

Customer-facing account statements over a double-entry {{:https://github.com/winterchill-trading/ledger}ledger}:
one account in one currency over a calendar month or up to twelve months of whole UTC
days, with running balances, two ways of presenting card and payment holds, and
localised CSV and PDF rendering.

{1 Where to start}

- {!Statements.Period}: months and day ranges, and the validation of a statement
  request.
- {!Statements.Statement}: the statement itself, built from journal records in memory
  or streamed from a journal file, with {!Statements.Statement.check} for its
  identities.
- {!Statements.Basis}: holds netted (the customer view) or every posting (the book
  view).
- {!Statements.Annotation}: descriptions, counterparties and categories supplied by the
  caller.
- {!Statements.Catalogue} and {!Statements.Locale}: labels, numbers and dates in six
  languages.
- {!Statements.Csv} and {!Statements.Pdf}: the two renderings.
- {!Statements.Pdf_writer}, {!Statements.Pdf_font}, {!Statements.Truetype},
  {!Statements.Win_ansi}: the small PDF toolkit underneath, usable for other documents
  such as receipts.

{1 Example}

The program [examples/quickstart.ml] in the repository builds a journal with a deposit,
a settled card payment and a pending one, and renders the month's statement; CI builds
and runs it.

{[
  let statement =
    Statements.Statement.create
      records
      ~account:customer
      ~currency:Money.Currency.eur
      ~period:(Statements.Period.of_month { year = 2026; month = Oct })
      ~basis:Netted
      ~now
    |> ok_exn
  in
  let csv = Statements.Csv.render statement in
  let pdf =
    Statements.Pdf.render
      ~catalogue:(Statements.Catalogue.builtin De)
      ~header:(Statements.Pdf.Header.create ~account_name:"Girokonto" ())
      statement
  in
  ...
]}
